@meta
id: 19-11
title: Teach vim your grep
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: vimgrep
par: 44
minutes: 5
vscode: the "files to include" box, filled in every time
vimrc: set grepprg=grep\ -rn\ --include=*.ts\ $*\ src nohidden
open: docs/logging.md

@brief
Every time you type `:grep -r ... src` you are re-typing the same
shape. The `grepprg` option is that shape, saved. It holds the command
line vim runs, with `$*` standing for whatever you type after `:grep`.
This lesson's vimrc sets it to `grep -rn --include=*.ts $* src`, so
`:grep logger.debug` runs `grep -rn --include=*.ts logger.debug src`:
recursive, line-numbered, TypeScript only, under `src`. `grepformat` is
the companion option that tells vim how to read the output; the default
already understands the `file:line:text` that `-n` produces.

The job: the incident is over and every `logger.debug(` call under
`src` goes, whole line. There is one in `docs/logging.md`, open in
front of you, as an example of how the logger is used. It is
documentation and stays, and with this `grepprg` it is never in the
list. The `debug` method itself, in `logger.ts`, stays too.

`:cdo` runs any command, not just `s`. `:d` deletes a line.

@keys
| `grepprg` | the command `:grep` runs; `$*` is your arguments |
| `grepformat` | how vim reads the output; the default handles `file:line:text` |
| `:cdo d \| update` | delete each hit's line, write |

@hints
`:grep logger.debug`. Nothing else; the option supplies the rest. It
is a grep regex, so the dot matches any character, which here is fine.
--
`:cdo d | update`. Then `:q`.

@solution
    :grep logger.debug<Enter>  :cdo d | update<Enter>  :q<Enter>

The option line for your own vimrc, when you have ripgrep installed:

    set grepprg=rg\ --vimgrep grepformat=%f:%l:%c:%m

`rg --vimgrep` prints `file:line:col:text` and respects `.gitignore`,
so `node_modules` never turns up. The backslashes escape the spaces,
which `:set` would otherwise read as the start of the next option.
`:grep` uses `grepprg`; `:vimgrep` never does.

`:cdo d` is worth a second look. Deleting a line shifts everything
below it, and the second hit in the order provider was below the first.
Vim adjusts the remaining entries in a buffer when its lines move, so
the second `d` landed on the right line. That adjustment holds for any
edit you make while a list is live, which is what makes walking a list
and editing as you go safe.

@start docs/logging.md
# Logging

Inject `Logger` and call `this.logger.info` for anything an operator
might need. `this.logger.debug('cache miss', { key })` is for local
investigation only and should not reach main.

@start src/infrastructure/logger.ts
export type LogEntry = {
  level: 'debug' | 'info' | 'error';
  message: string;
  context?: Record<string, unknown>;
};

export class Logger {
  public write(entry: LogEntry) {
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(entry) + '\n');
  }

  public info(message: string, context?: Record<string, unknown>) {
    this.write({ level: 'info', message, context });
  }

  public debug(message: string, context?: Record<string, unknown>) {
    this.write({ level: 'debug', message, context });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);
    this.logger.debug('cancel: loaded', { id, status: order.status });

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    this.logger.debug('cancel: refunded', { id });
    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/payment/payment.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PaymentRepository } from './payment.repository';
import { PaymentProducer } from './payment.producer';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class PaymentProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(PaymentRepository) protected paymentRepository: PaymentRepository,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async reverse(id: string) {
    const payment = await this.paymentRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!payment) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const receipt = await this.paymentService.sendRefund(payment.orderId);
    this.logger.debug('reverse: gateway receipt', { receipt });

    await this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: id, receipt });

    return receipt;
  }
}

@expected src/domain/payment/payment.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PaymentRepository } from './payment.repository';
import { PaymentProducer } from './payment.producer';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class PaymentProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(PaymentRepository) protected paymentRepository: PaymentRepository,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async reverse(id: string) {
    const payment = await this.paymentRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!payment) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const receipt = await this.paymentService.sendRefund(payment.orderId);

    await this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: id, receipt });

    return receipt;
  }
}

@start src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async sendRefund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post('/sendRefund', { orderId });
    this.logger.debug('gateway status', { status: response.status });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async sendRefund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post('/sendRefund', { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}
